# Rust build artifacts
# The entire target directory contains generated build artifacts
# and should never be committed. This includes:
# - Compiled binaries and libraries
# - Generated documentation (target/doc/)
# - Debug information and symbols
# - Incremental compilation cache
/target/
**/target/

# Cargo.lock for libraries (keep for applications)
# For libraries: typically ignored (let consumers choose versions)
# For applications: should be committed (ensure reproducible builds)
# Since CameoDB is a database system (application), we keep Cargo.lock
# Cargo.lock

